      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing a Provider**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud Pub/Sub for publishing the JSON event. The next step is to integrate its unique identifier within the `publish_event.py` file to ensure proper operation.\n\n\n**Defining the Function**\n\nI'm now creating `publish_event.py`. The focus is a function taking a topic name and JSON message as input. I'm leveraging the Google Cloud Pub/Sub client library. Imports and client initialization are coming next to ensure that the provider's unique identifier is present in this setup.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789866613833,
          "start": 1789866612542
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc5d173e001gnrQtajwCmUKLe",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc5d123a001eNJwYwYd2Imi3X",
      "session_id": "ses_f43a2ee46ffeAZUzypRG3T39En",
      "time_created": 1789866612542,
      "time_updated": 1789866613833
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "yIi7o5SyvjPjgie6",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import json\nimport os\nfrom google.cloud import pubsub_v1\n\ndef publish_json_event(project_id: str, topic_id: str, message: dict) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Publishes a JSON message to a Google Cloud Pub/Sub topic.\"\"\"\n    publisher = pubsub_v1.PublisherClient()\n    topic_path = publisher.topic_path(project_id, topic_id)\n\n    # Data must be a bytestring\n    data = json.dumps(message).encode(\"utf-8\")\n\n    future = publisher.publish(topic_path, data)\n    print(f\"Published message ID: {future.result()}\")\n    return future.result()\n\n",
            "filePath": "publish_event.py"
          },
